Postulate 3: Weaving Hierarchy

Material structures consist of topological knots (non-automatically dissociable weaved subgraphs) organized in recursive hierarchies. Interactions between topological knots are mediated through shared links. Each element of this recursive growth tree is a topological knot of a specific order, whose total number of primitive bricks is determined by that of its parent knots.

