Theorem 8.1 (Geometric Enforcement of Pauli Exclusion): Two identical electron bricks cannot occupy exactly the same geometric position and phase state.

Proof: If two identical electron bricks occupy exactly the same geometric state, the exchange operation reduces to the identity operation (0 reconnection steps, even). But Lemma 8.1 requires the exchange reconnection number to be odd. The contradiction that an odd number equals an even number forces the assumption to be false. Two identical electron bricks must maintain at least one degree of freedom difference—either a phase difference 
