Definition 8.3: Baryon Brick and Binary Layered Structure

At an order much higher than the electron brick in the recursive growth tree, there exist giant stable topological knots composed of large numbers of electron bricks and deeper-level primitive bricks, woven according to recursive rules.

The structure of such topological knots exhibits a universal binary layered pattern:

Solid core: composed of a large number of electron bricks or equivalent primitive bricks in the densest packing arrangement. For macroscopic topological knots, cubic close packing is the optimal arrangement, with the number of core primitive bricks approaching integer multiples of 
