Characteristics:

Fission probability depends on the stress distribution among the suture lines inside the nuclide. The more concentrated the stress on a suture line and the closer it is to the edge tolerance limit, the higher the fission probability of that nuclide.

Fission probability is one of the three key factors determining whether a nuclide can persist in nature (see Part V, three-factor criterion).

