8.4 Accelerated Cosmic Expansion
The topological tension coupling between the membrane and the external substrate continuously injects energy during membrane expansion, driving accelerated expansion.

Phenomenologically, this continuous energy injection manifests as the accelerated expansion of the universe—i.e., the observational effect attributed to dark energy in the standard model. No new field or new entity is required.

8.5 Elemental Abundance Distribution
The cyclic dynamics (aggregation–fission cycles) of leapfrog paths, integrated over time, produce the observed elemental abundance distribution. Every particle is an intermediate product of time and probability.

8.6 High-Redshift Massive Structures
Leapfrog paths allow direct aggregation in the early membrane to form massive topological stars. No seed black holes with prolonged accretion are needed. This naturally explains the massive galaxies observed by JWST at high redshifts (
